":"China's central bank held loan rates steady for the 17th month: 1-yr LPR 3.00%, 5-yr 3.50%. Plain-language take: after Q3 GDP beat at 4.5%, Beijing feels no urgency to cut. The 5-yr rate anchors mortgages, so holding it = no new push for the housing market for now. Instead, the","url":"https://x.com/TXPOTATO/status/2112556711374368908"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["13_2112398989064855552"]},"author_id":"2095760865232560128","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:22:55.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112399136276558197"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/n7kARVNMkT","end":249,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/LSN_NEWS_WORLD/status/2112399136276558197/video/1","media_key":"13_2112398989064855552","start":226,"url":"https://t.co/n7kARVNMkT"}]},"id":"2112399136276558197","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":8,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"China grew 4.5% in Q3, beating forecasts. Retail sales +1.1%, property investment -20.6% this year. Yuan at its strongest since 2022. PBOC held the LPR for a 17th month.\n\nAsia Money Map: a factory number, not a family number. https://t.co/n7kARVNMkT","url":"https://x.com/LSN_NEWS_WORLD/status/2112399136276558197"},{"author_id":"1883321599153373185","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:25:29.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112399781439869085"],"id":"2112399781439869085","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":14,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"🇨🇳 CHINA'S CENTRAL BANK\n🏦 The People's Bank of China left its loan prime rates unchanged today.\n🇨🇳 1-year LPR: 3.00%.\n🇨🇳 5-year LPR: 3.50%.\n📌 The decision is in line with market expectations.\n📈 China's economy grew 4.5% year-on-year in the third quarter.\n📉 However, weakness","url":"https://x.com/pipmoment/status/2112399781439869085"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2112732792828137472"]},"author_id":"1092889720181407745","created_at":"2026-10-21T02:28:49.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112732809399779804"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/C2r6j2qMkK","end":299,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/AfricaisHOME2/status/2112732809399779804/photo/1","media_key":"3_2112732792828137472","start":276,"url":"https://t.co/C2r6j2qMkK"}]},"id":"2112732809399779804","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":1,"impression_count":38,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"China has kept its benchmark lending rates unchanged for the 17th consecutive month in October 2026, maintaining stability in borrowing costs as policymakers assess the country’s economic performance. The People’s Bank of China (PBOC) held the one-year loan prime rate (LPR), https://t.co/C2r6j2qMkK","url":"https://x.com/AfricaisHOME2/status/2112732809399779804"},{"author_id":"1244266306485932034","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:25:32.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112354495401508909"],"entities":{"cashtags":[{"end":150,"start":143,"tag":"SHCOMP"},{"end":156,"start":151,"tag":"SSEC"},{"end":162,"start":157,"tag":"ASHR"},{"end":220,"start":215,"tag":"KWEB"},{"end":225,"start":221,"tag":"FXI"},{"end":230,"start":226,"tag":"HXC"},{"end":236,"start":231,"tag":"DRAG"},{"end":242,"start":237,"tag":"YINN"},{"end":248,"start":243,"tag":"YANG"}],"hashtags":[{"end":142,"start":136,"tag":"CHINA"},{"end":261,"start":249,"tag":"STOCKMARKET"}]},"id":"2112354495401508909","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":1,"impression_count":8951,"like_count":11,"quote_count":1,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":1},"text":"🇨🇳LPR unchanged in October\nThe PBOC left the one-year and five-year loan prime rates (LPR) unchanged at 3.00% and 3.50%, respectively.  #CHINA $SHCOMP $SSEC $ASHR solana:3aSu9uuDLiWkBQGycJDDSubZEPb6YJjDzULPWZkJn8ic $KWEB $FXI $HXC $DRAG $YINN $YANG #STOCKMARKET","url":"https://x.com/Sino_Market/status/2112354495401508909"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2112534966718324736"]},"author_id":"2043043072745897985","created_at":"2026-10-20T18:45:00.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112616087162683474"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/amRn80V78c","end":303,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/HangingContext/status/2112616087162683474/photo/1","media_key":"3_2112534966718324736","start":280,"url":"https://t.co/amRn80V78c"}]},"id":"2112616087162683474","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":77,"like_count":0,"quote_count":1,"reply_count":1,"retweet_count":0},"text":"China rewired its rate machinery this week — then courted global capital in the same breath.\n\nThe PBOC will move loan pricing off the single LPR benchmark, shift open-market operations toward overnight, and set up a liquidity backstop for non-bank redemptions. Then it opened RMB https://t.co/amRn80V78c","url":"https://x.com/HangingContext/status/2112616087162683474"},{"author_id":"2009430739096584192","created_at":"2026-10-20T18:27:16.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112611623978651722"],"id":"2112611623978651722","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":9,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"The PBOC held the LPR for a 17th straight month. But overnight repo averages about 1.25%, 15bp below the 1.40% seven-day rate. Making it the main policy rate would formalize easing without a headline cut. PPI at 5.0% does not change that. CPI is 0.9%.","url":"https://x.com/macro_soup/status/2112611623978651722"},{"author_id":"364720480","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:03:04.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112379042980933962"],"id":"2112379042980933962","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":125,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"El LPR de China quedó sin cambios en octubre: el PBOC mantuvo las tasas de referencia a un año y a cinco años en 3,00% y 3,50% respectivamente.","url":"https://x.com/cacus/status/2112379042980933962"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2112393146726486017","3_2112393148710457344","3_2112393152724357120"]},"author_id":"1409680